      "text": "Every country has its strengths — and its pressure points.\n\nIndia — Wage growth vs. rising living costs  \nIsrael — Ongoing security concerns  \nUSA — Political polarization  \nUK — High tax burden & cost of living  \nRussia — Sanctions & global isolation  \nPakistan — Job scarcity & security issues  \nChina — Surveillance & information controls  \nJapan — Aging population & shrinking workforce  \nSyria — Conflict & humanitarian crisis  \nUkraine — War & economic disruption  \nIran — Personal freedoms & sanctions pressure  \nEgypt — Currency instability & inflation  \nPhilippines — Limited access to high-paying jobs  \nLebanon — Financial system breakdown  \nFrance — Social unrest & labor disputes  \nNigeria — Governance & corruption challenges  \nGermany — Regulation & slowing growth  \nCanada — Housing affordability crisis  \n\nNo nation is problem-free — the real question is how each one adapts.",
